 "story": "Arctic tundra is treeless land frozen below the surface. In summer the thawed top layer turns to marsh and lakes, and millions of birds arrive. Caribou and geese eat sedges, snowy owls hunt lemmings, and wolves hunt caribou and muskoxen.",
 "matters": "Permafrost stores huge amounts of carbon. As it thaws it releases carbon dioxide and methane, which warm the Arctic further and speed up the thaw."
